.TH AVR\-REPO\-MIRROR\-CLUSTERS 1 "" "avr 0.2.0" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-repo-mirror-clusters \- List the git clusters a mirror can be placed in.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr repo mirror clusters
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
List the git clusters a mirror can be placed in.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Examples:
    avr repo mirror clusters
    avr repo mirror clusters --json cluster_id,datacenter_id
.fi
.RE
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
JSON FIELDS
    cluster_id, datacenter_id, name
.fi
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug. Uses default org if not specified (see: avr config set org).
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR \fITEXT\fR
Output JSON. Pass comma-separated field names, "*" for all fields, or "?" to list available fields.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-jq\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter --json output through a jq expression.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr (1),
.BR avr-repo-mirror (1),
.BR avr-repo-mirror-disable (1),
.BR avr-repo-mirror-enable (1),
.BR avr-repo-mirror-place (1),
.BR avr-repo-mirror-status (1),
.BR avr-repo-mirror-unplace (1)
